I had a similar situation in the Sanctum in a recent game,
only I was burdened as well. I opted for the blessed
unihorn. I got lucky and it cured the sickness and the
stunning and then I got a breather when Demogorgon took a
fancy for the priest's amulet and I could reorganize. There
was a recent YAAP where the poster relied entirely on his
blessed unihorn while fighting Demogorgon.

Don't neglect other healing opportunities, prayer and
uncursed !oEH and FH, even a eucalyptus leaf. Prayer might
cure the illness and stunning at once.

I tried teleporting him away and gave up after about three
tries, but later got it to work in wiz mode. A ?oEarth might
save you here. A ?oSM might as well.

Demogorgon's speed is 15 and you are faster than that, I
forget, either 18 or 20 with speed boots. The point is,
you'll sometimes get a free move to cure and get down an
Elbereth. If you ever get down the first Elbereth, you'll
have the advantage. If you are cured but still stunned you
might try moving, if this is when you get your free turn you
can escape and if you blunder into him maybe he will go to
the stairs to heal.
